 "description": "P3 of PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_PLAN.md: the construction-codebook sd loop for kind 'prog_construction' -- a PARALLEL decode loop over hub-IR statement observations, following seeds/role_decode_loop.json's precedent (a sibling loop for a new kind; seeds/shape_decode_loop.json is FROZEN and untouched -- this seed uses its OWN pc_* status attrs, its OWN prog_codebook_epoch on the Agent, and namespaced relation predicates pstmt/parg/pop/parity/pblock, so neither loop can see the other's work: the frozen loop's rules key on the 'status' attr these Observations never carry, and no other codebook's signatures share these predicates, so literal cover cannot cross kinds). The ladder, Occam-ordered within one run_rules fixpoint: pcon_decode (literal ShapeDecode) -> pcon_recognize (empty residual: exact/compositional cover, no growth) -> pcon_recognize_covered (a WILDCARDED merged quantum whole-signature-Covers the observation -- the standalone Covers Term, pattern-side wilds match; needed because the literal ShapeDecode cover can never match a part-side WILD, a measured engine fact recorded in PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_P3_PREREG.md par.2) -> pcon_mark_merge (MERGE-AT-MINT, the NEW piece: the 2/3-leaf-fix MDL join criterion in integer form, verdict marked on the Observation, application mechanical in the driver) -> pcon_mint (only when nothing covers and nothing joins; bounded Term-computed name; in-rule epoch bump) -> pcon_redecode (growth re-arms observations decoded under an older prog_codebook_epoch). Gates: tests/test_prog_constructions_migrated.py. RULE-NAME NAMESPACE: rules are pcon_* (not pc_*) because seeds/ls20_percell.json already owns a rule literally named pc_mint -- a name collision with rule-name-keyed machinery (e.g. the daemon's per-name rule refresh) is avoided by construction; the MINTED QUANTA keep the pc_ name prefix (node names, a different namespace).",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "prog_construction_loop",
  "description": "a program statement's IR shape decodes against the held construction codebook; a residual joins a near quantum by anti-unification (merge-at-mint) or mints a new one; the run_rules fixpoint is the decode->grow->re-decode loop, at code-construction grain."
